<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">County Tipperary</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">County Tipperary is an inland county in the province of Munster, in southern Ireland, crossed by the River Suir. It contains the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rock-of-cashel">Rock of Cashel</a>, seat of the kings of Munster, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-cross-abbey">Holy Cross Abbey</a>. From 1328 much of it formed a palatinate of the Butler earls of Ormond, which was abolished in 1716.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/county-tipperary.jpg" alt="County Tipperary" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Island_of_Ireland_location_map.svg: *Ireland_location_map.svg: NordNordWest Northern_Ireland_location_map.svg: NordNo... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Island_of_Ireland_location_map_Tipperary.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
